  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 244 AM EDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nA quasi stationary front has drifted SE little more than 100\nmiles with a moist and somewhat unstable airmass south of it and\ndrier, more stable to the north. Widely scattered showers\ncontinue to percolate across the area with very slow overall\nmovement as a weak wave moves through. Confidence in precip \nchances through the next 24 to 36 hours remains quite low as any\nincrease in convection will need assistance of additional weak \ndisturbances. Eventually, the front looks to slowly washout\nlater Friday/Friday night. CAMs are all over the place with pops\nand QPF. Given the concerns noted, have continued with slgt chc\nto chc pops into Friday and defer any increase to later\nforecasts if trends become clearer. PWATs of 1.75\" or higher\nwill yield a small risk of heavy rainfall, with areas that see\ntraining showers/storms seeing some limited flooding concerns\npossible. WPC has maintained the Marginal Risk for Excessive\nRainfall. \n\nThere may be a lull in precip chances later Friday into Sunday,\nbut eventually another boundary will setup across the region\nwith increasing chances for showers and storms returning. While\nchc to likely pops exist in the later periods, confidence on\nlocation, timing and coverage remain low this far out.",
